        "2": {
            "name": "text_block",
            "id": 311,
            "position_x": 862,
            "position_y": 45,
            "width": 768,
            "height": 916,
            "visibility": "show_all",
            "draggable": true,
            "presentation_state": "show_all",
            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Sorts values into bins marked by a list of edges, and gives each value the number of its bin. With edges -0.5 0 0.5, anything below -0.5 is bin 0, -0.5 up to 0 is bin 1, 0 up to 0.5 is bin 2, and 0.5 or more is bin 3.\n\nUse it to turn a continuous control into steps or zones - a fader into one of five scenes, a hand's height into low, middle and high, a speed into still, slow, fast - with the boundaries wherever you want them, not evenly spaced. The bin numbers can then pick from a list with np.take, or route to outlets.\n\nSYNTAX:\nnp.digitize <edges: floats ...>\nDefault: no edges (send them to the edges inlet).\n\nEXAMPLE:\nnp.digitize 0.2 0.4 0.8\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nin:\nThe values: a number, list or array of any shape. Every input is sorted and sent.\n\nedges:\nThe bin boundaries, in increasing (or decreasing) order, replacing any given as arguments. Held: send them first. N edges make N + 1 bins, numbered 0 to N.\n\nright:\nAn option, under the node. Off (the default), a value exactly on an edge goes into the bin above it; on, into the bin below.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nbin indices:\nThe bin number of each value, the shape of the input.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\nTop: a sine wave from -1 to 1 through edges -0.5 0 0.5 becomes a staircase of 0 1 2 3 - flat while the wave stays inside a zone, stepping as it crosses an edge. The outer steps are wider than the inner ones because the wave lingers near its peaks.\n\nBottom: -0.9 -0.2 0.3 0.8 fall in bins 0 1 2 3.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.histogram counts how many values fall in each bin. np.take turns bin numbers into values. round and floor make evenly spaced steps.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 760,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
                    "value": 900,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "4": {
                    "name": "text_size",
                    "value": "30",
                    "value_type": "str"
                }
            },
            "text": "Sorts values into bins marked by a list of edges, and gives each value the number of its bin. With edges -0.5 0 0.5, anything below -0.5 is bin 0, -0.5 up to 0 is bin 1, 0 up to 0.5 is bin 2, and 0.5 or more is bin 3.\n\nUse it to turn a continuous control into steps or zones - a fader into one of five scenes, a hand's height into low, middle and high, a speed into still, slow, fast - with the boundaries wherever you want them, not evenly spaced. The bin numbers can then pick from a list with np.take, or route to outlets.\n\nSYNTAX:\nnp.digitize <edges: floats ...>\nDefault: no edges (send them to the edges inlet).\n\nEXAMPLE:\nnp.digitize 0.2 0.4 0.8\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nin:\nThe values: a number, list or array of any shape. Every input is sorted and sent.\n\nedges:\nThe bin boundaries, in increasing (or decreasing) order, replacing any given as arguments. Held: send them first. N edges make N + 1 bins, numbered 0 to N.\n\nright:\nAn option, under the node. Off (the default), a value exactly on an edge goes into the bin above it; on, into the bin below.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nbin indices:\nThe bin number of each value, the shape of the input.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\nTop: a sine wave from -1 to 1 through edges -0.5 0 0.5 becomes a staircase of 0 1 2 3 - flat while the wave stays inside a zone, stepping as it crosses an edge. The outer steps are wider than the inner ones because the wave lingers near its peaks.\n\nBottom: -0.9 -0.2 0.3 0.8 fall in bins 0 1 2 3.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.histogram counts how many values fall in each bin. np.take turns bin numbers into values. round and floor make evenly spaced steps."
        },
